NCCL 2.27 doesn't support all features yet, e.g. device pointers for symmetric memory.
This leads to CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS errors in some kernels.

Let it throw an exception instead of silently returning NULL pointers, and add a test skip for this case.
See https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/185216

Author: Alexander Grund (TU Dresden)

